    "recommendations": "Reducing direct vegetation contact with the structure by clearing brush and shrubs adjacent to exterior walls and foundation areas could meaningfully improve the immediate defensible space zone. Where tree clusters exist near improvements, increasing horizontal separation between individual trees and between trees and the structure may reduce fuel continuity and limit pathways for fire spread. Scattered shrubs and mixed vegetation across the property should be managed to reduce connectivity between surface fuels and any elevated canopy fuels present in tree clusters. Vegetation growing along the access route should be trimmed back to maintain clearance and support firefighter access and suppression operations. Preserving and expanding existing irrigated landscaping near the structure could further support defensible space by creating lower-fuel buffer areas. Where defensible space is already established, continued routine maintenance of those zones would support long-term wildfire resilience and help sustain the separation that currently exists between fuels and improvements."
